      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DEADLINE (2) gets top billing in a moderate NR up to 33 despite finishing last at Riverina Paceway first-up, as he has proven distance form and this looks no harder than the NR up to 36 he met there. The concern is that he was beaten a long way and has a recent head-to-head margin to overturn on GLAMOUR FOX, but with a good draw he may produce more second-up. OKTOLOVE (3) is hard to trust on two Kilmore failures, including being tailed off last start, but the drop from NR up to 38 and his three wins at this track and distance make him a threat. ROCKIN CHARMER (5) also brings poor last-start figures, yet the drop from NR up to 42 is the strongest class angle in the race and he can improve sharply if he finds anything like his better form. GLAMOUR FOX (6) is the steadier each-way option after being beaten only six and a half metres at Young, with Peter McRae's strong record aboard her adding enough substance to her claims.",
